Z||000013||fiero56||04-24-2001||09:58 PM||||Eric, do you have a source for '88 rebuilt m/c that are in-stock? Every shop here has to order. If there is a shop there with them in stock, I would drive over and pick one up tommorrow to try and finish this.<P>BTW, those were my next questions.||||reg||1
Z||000014||theogre||04-24-2001||11:05 PM||||For reference... All Fiero's and nearly all GM product in the last 20 years, use the step bore MC. Even most of the cross fed systems on FWD have it.<P>88 has a 24mm main bore while the older ones are 25.4mm. the large rear bore is 36mm on both. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Eric||04-25-2001||12:45 AM||||Yeah, I knew the design was a little different (bore is level to the ground on 88s), but was fundamentally the same.<P>56, I've been getting the master cylinders from Advanced.  They took my core and gave me one that looked exactly like it.  It was aluminum just like the original.  Each time I've had to order it, so it takes like a day or two to get in.||||reg||1
